  "scope": "An actual fixed 80-instruction endpoint-retention primitive reads the represented zero flag and executes the original padded numeric comparison on source and, when necessary, target labels. Nonzero-cost vertices short-circuit to kept; zero-cost endpoints remain kept. The same-run theorem preserves original labels/context and returns the exact old kept-adjacency vertex predicate, with a word-length-only physical bound including final halt. Eight actual physical cases cover both endpoints, padded equal labels, neither endpoint, duplicate endpoints and the short-circuit path. Initial context/flag/label representations and address widths remain explicit. Constructing the whole retained mask and adjacency matrix, integrating the actual zero-mask result and running full outer dispatch remain separate.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
